WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:04.375
- I recently told somebody that
getting attacked by a shark

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:05.615
was the greatest thing
that's ever happened to me.

00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:07.743
And they're like, "That's absurd.”

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:10.022
“You know, why would you say that?"

00:00:10.022 --> 00:00:11.403
I've had incredible opportunities.

00:00:11.403 --> 00:00:13.687
I've been able to visit
some really cool places

00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:16.400
and meet some incredible people.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.567
All these things have been
nurtured from this shark attack.

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:25.141
I think it's really
made me who I am today.

00:00:25.141 --> 00:00:28.308
(driving piano music)

00:00:30.472 --> 00:00:31.453
My name is Mike Coots.

00:00:31.453 --> 00:00:33.857
I live on the island of Kauai in Hawaii.

00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:37.128
I'm a surfer, photographer,
and shark attack survivor.

00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:39.019
There's some really great
surf spots out here.

00:00:39.019 --> 00:00:42.062
I was 18 years old, surfing
here on Kauai with some friends,

00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:44.776
and it was early in the
morning and I paddled out

00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:46.447
and thought I was gonna
have a surf session

00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:49.126
like any other day, and
it was a lot different.

00:00:49.126 --> 00:00:51.089
I got attacked by a tiger shark.

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:51.922
As soon as I hit it,

00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:54.085
it let go and disappeared back underwater.

00:00:54.085 --> 00:00:56.146
And I remember passing out

00:00:56.146 --> 00:00:57.704
basically as soon as
we got to the hospital

00:00:57.704 --> 00:01:01.704
and I woke up a day-and-a-half
later an amputee.

00:01:03.151 --> 00:01:08.143
I got my first prosthetic six
months after the shark attack.

00:01:08.143 --> 00:01:09.760
Early on, you think you can't do this,

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.042
you think you can't do that.

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:13.861
You know, there's these physical
limitations on life.

00:01:13.861 --> 00:01:15.707
And I didn't think I could drive
a truck with a stick shift.

00:01:15.707 --> 00:01:17.672
And you learn how to drive
a truck with a stick shift

00:01:17.672 --> 00:01:19.296
and you're like, "Wow, that was cool."

00:01:19.296 --> 00:01:22.035
And you build up these little
things like day to day to day.

00:01:22.035 --> 00:01:23.610
After a while, it's like bring it on.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.919
What can happen that I
can't figure out how to do?

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.982
I was in college and I
remember class got out.

00:01:29.982 --> 00:01:30.815
I was like, "You know what?”

00:01:30.815 --> 00:01:32.002
"I'm gonna take a longboard;

00:01:32.002 --> 00:01:33.104
I'm gonna get the
biggest board I can find

00:01:33.104 --> 00:01:34.749
and just take my prosthetic in the water

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:36.413
and see what happens."

00:01:36.413 --> 00:01:39.550
I caught a wave and I was
screaming pretty loud.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.383
I was like, "What?!”

00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:41.743
"This is cool; this is amazing!"

00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:43.684
And I think that was the best wave

00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:46.101
I had ever caught in my life.

00:01:47.185 --> 00:01:48.602
From then on, I started figuring out,

00:01:48.602 --> 00:01:49.489
okay, what's gonna break?

00:01:49.489 --> 00:01:50.954
What can I make that's a foot

00:01:50.954 --> 00:01:52.375
that'll help me surf even better?

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:55.940
And trying to basically make
the ultimate surfing foot.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.626
I think I'm doing it because it's fun,

00:01:57.626 --> 00:01:59.612
but I’m also, it's this learning experience

00:01:59.612 --> 00:02:01.818
and it's taking this
information and passing it on

00:02:01.818 --> 00:02:05.485
to people that wanna
surf with a prosthetic.

00:02:06.495 --> 00:02:07.651
The ocean has taken a lot from me,

00:02:07.651 --> 00:02:10.521
but what it's given back to
me has been immeasurable.

00:02:10.521 --> 00:02:13.320
I've lost, you know, nearly my life to a shark,

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.874
yet I really believe sharks are one of the

00:02:16.874 --> 00:02:19.826
if not the most important
species in our marine ecosystem.

00:02:19.826 --> 00:02:21.685
And at the rate that
they're being killed off,

00:02:21.685 --> 00:02:24.317
they're not gonna be
around in 10, 15, 20 years.

00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:25.799
And why not use something that could,

00:02:25.799 --> 00:02:29.352
I guess, be said as a negative
and turn it into a positive.

00:02:29.352 --> 00:02:30.442
The shark attack's been the greatest thing

00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:31.765
that's ever happened to me.

00:02:31.765 --> 00:02:34.515
(slow pop music)

